{
  "schema": "starcrew.names/1",
  "_doc": "Officer and crew names (openspec/changes/lobby design 2; read by sc-core::names). A style is a pattern of {part}s, and each part is a list of syllable slots: one syllable is drawn from each slot in turn and joined (an empty string makes a slot optional). A style is drawn by its weight. Names are built from syllables, never taken from a series: a generated name equal to an entry of `deny` (canon characters, checked case-blind against the whole name and each word of it) is drawn again. Take the shape, not the text (CLAUDE.md 15).",
